{'symbol': 'ON', 'date': '2020-03-06 11:30:00', 'title': 'ON SEMICONDUCTOR UPDATES FIRST QUARTER 2020 REVENUE OUTLOOK', 'text': 'ON SEMICONDUCTOR UPDATES FIRST QUARTER 2020 REVENUE OUTLOOK.SEES Q1 2020 REVENUE $1.275 BILLION TO $1.325 BILLION.UPDATE INCORPORATES POTENTIAL IMPACT OF CHANGE IN BUSINESS CONDITIONS DUE TO NOVEL CORONAVIRUS KNOWN AS COVID-19..INTENDS TO TAKE RESTRUCTURING MEASURES DURING Q1 OF 2020 TO REALIGN ITS INVESTMENTS..RESTRUCTURING MEASURES ARE EXPECTED TO RESULT IN ANNUAL COST SAVINGS OF APPROXIMATELY $90 MILLION.ON SEMICONDUCTOR - FACTORIES IN CHINA HAVE RETURNED TO NORMAL LEVELS OF OPERATIONS AFTER MANDATORY SHUTDOWN FOLLOWING END OF LUNAR NEW YEAR HOLIDAYS.SAW SOFT ORDER TRENDS IN CHINA IN WEEKS FOLLOWING LUNAR NEW YEAR HOLIDAYS, BUT ORDERS HAVE SINCE PICKED UP.COMPANY EXPECTS TO ACHIEVE TARGETED COST SAVINGS BY END OF 2020 ON QUARTERLY RUN RATE BASIS.'}